    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to exploit several high-ceiling matchups today, led by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (77.82). **Gunnar Henderson** represents our most compelling start; facing Bailey Ober, his elite projection is bolstered by an impressive 19% SP skill advantage and a \"slow delivery\" flag, which significantly boosts his stolen base potential in a category where we remain hyper-aggressive. Similarly, **Luis Robert Jr.** (76.18) finds himself in an excellent spot against a soft matchup, benefiting from a 14% platoon edge as he hits out of the four-hole. We are also leaning heavily on **Kyle Tucker** (73.86) and **Jacob Wilson** (72.73), both of whom capitalize on favorable park factors and high SP-xERA targets, ensuring our lineup remains productive across the 5x5 categories.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Jackson Merrill** (38.94), who sits on the bench after failing to clear our 40.0 efficiency floor. While his talent is undeniable, he faces a tough assignment against Harrison and a severe negative platoon disadvantage, which caused his projection to crater relative to our other utility options. Consequently, we opted to roll with **Miguel Vargas** (63.34) in the UTIL spot, as his strong xwOBA (0.379) and superior matchup against Nick Lodolo provided a safer, higher-upside floor. While **Nasim Nunez** (48.11) was considered for his speed profile, the combination of a difficult matchup against Shota Imanaga and a lower order spot ultimately pushed him out of the starting nine. We will continue to monitor **Drake Baldwin** and **Heliot Ramos**, as both are hovering near the marginal threshold, but we are confident that today's configuration maximizes our run production and stolen base probability.",
